  "poll_seconds": 15,
  "dark_buffer_seconds": 30,
  "green_repeat_seconds": 900,

  "_wg": "Liveness signal that PARSES OUT SLEEP. Set wg_interface to the phone's WireGuard iface on the router (e.g. wg0) and set Persistent Keepalive = 25 on the phone's peer in the Flint 2 GUI. Then a sleeping-but-connected phone still counts as alive; only a truly-down tunnel goes dark. wg_peer optional: the phone's public key, to isolate it if other peers share the iface. Leave wg_interface empty to fall back to DNS-activity liveness (trips on normal sleep).",
  "wg_interface": "wg0",
  "wg_peer": "",

